{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"HARNESS DEFECT THAT FLATTERED REBAR. supplement_aggregate.py collected judges with a glob that also matched the worklist file, so the worklist was read as a fourth judge on every panel. Class votes were protected by an existing guard, but the link-vote append was unconditional, giving every item a phantom no-link vote. Majority linkage is computed against the vote count, so a genuine 2-of-3 link scored 2*2 > 4 as false and was dropped. Dropping a link moves its item into the rebar-unique metric and leaves its adjudicated issue in the missed metric. A phantom no-link vote can only ever remove a link, never add one, so the bug was one-directional toward overstating rebar's uniqueness. Measured effect: one link recovered. A second latent failure never fired: the panel-completeness gate also counted the worklist, so a two-judge panel would have passed and been aggregated on plurality. Fixed both."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789442986626838001,"uuid":"6897a4fb-071b-4022-84c7-11406ad20039"}